<title>JAPAN: JAPAN BUYS 120,000 TONNES WHEAT, 30,000 T BARLEY.</title>
<headline>JAPAN BUYS 120,000 TONNES WHEAT, 30,000 T BARLEY.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it bought 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat and 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat, and 30,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>They are all for October shipment. The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 60,000   Western white	   30,000</p>
<p>			     (Protein 13.5 pct)</p>
<p>			   Dark Northern Spring  20,000</p>
<p>			   Hard red winter	 10,000</p>
<p> Canada     40,000   1CW			 40,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000   Prime hard		20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Australia   30,000   Feed		     30,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
